# Regression fixture for inc-mc37. Player::AutoPickupFloor's unidentified-magic
# branch (src/Player.cpp) must NOT auto-stow an EF_MUNDANE item -- here holy
# water -- because EF_MUNDANE means "not magic" and the sweep is for magic.
# It must still stow real unidentified magic (the curate's healing potion).
# Read by tools/check_mundane_autopickup.sh.
#
# Route: an orc barbarian; wizard-summon a base human to the east; add the
# "curate" template, whose gear is a GUARANTEED 3d4 blessed flask of water
# (holy water, lib/mon2.irh) plus a 1d1 healing potion; genocide it so the pile
# drops on one tile; step onto the tile so AutoPickupFloor runs. @dump:before
# catches the loaded tile; @dump:after catches the view once the sweep settled.
# The holy water must REMAIN in view (not stowed); the potion must be gone
# (stowed), which proves the branch ran and still hoards real magic.
@include chargen.keys
w
y
@expect "Wizard Mode Options:"
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Humans"
@choose "Human"
RIGHT
ENTER
w
@choose "Add Template to Creature"
RIGHT
ENTER
@choose "Curate"
w
@choose "Genocide Everything"
RIGHT
@dump:before
SPACE
@dump:after
@quit
